<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Nature Gallery</title>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>🌿 Nature Gallery</h1>
  <p>Images help make webpages more attractive and informative. Below are some beautiful nature photographs.</p>

  <h2>Mountain View</h2>
  <img src="mountain.jpg" alt="Snow-covered mountains" width="400" height="300">
  <p>Tall mountains offer breathtaking views and attract visitors from around the world.</p>

  <h2>Forest Path</h2>
  <img src="forest.jpg" alt="A peaceful forest pathway" width="400" height="300">
  <p>Forests provide fresh air, wildlife habitats, and beautiful scenery.</p>

  <h2>Ocean Sunset</h2>
  <img src="ocean.jpg" alt="Sunset over the ocean" width="400" height="300">
  <p>Watching the sunset over the ocean is one of nature's most relaxing experiences.</p>

  <h2>Why Use Images?</h2>
  <p>The <strong>img</strong> tag allows us to display pictures on a webpage and make content more engaging.</p>

</body>
</html>
